  and [38;5;153mlogin()[39m is a stub that never calls [38;5;153mAPI_ENDPOINT[39m ([38;5;153mapp.js:4-8[39m). So "add a userId parameter" needs a source, and the
  three plausible sources give you three different functions.

  - [1mCaller-supplied identifier[0m — [38;5;153mlogin(userId, username, password)[39m. Buys exactly what you asked for; costs a new source
    for the value (a hidden form field, a tenant/account code, something from the page). Until that source exists the
    caller would pass [38;5;153mundefined[39m, so this only pays off if you already know where the value comes from. Signature is
    cheap to change now, expensive once other code calls it.
  - [1mClient-generated correlation ID[0m — [38;5;153mlogin()[39m mints a [38;5;153mcrypto.randomUUID()[39m per attempt and logs it. Buys traceability of
